Aether: manual-only updates, enforced in code

Updates are user-driven: the browser never looks for them on its own and
never downloads or installs anything by itself. The user asks for the
check (Help > About, or Preferences > "Check for updates"), the update is
offered, and only the user starts the download and the install.

This is enforced in code, not in configuration:

  - UpdateUtils.getAppUpdateAutoEnabled() always returns false, so the
    per-installation update-config.json, the app.update.auto pref and the
    app-auto-updates-* enterprise policies cannot turn automatic updates
    on. setAppUpdateAutoEnabled() keeps the setting off.
  - The policyFn hooks are gone from the per-installation update prefs:
    no policy takes part in the update configuration any more.
  - UpdateService no longer kicks off a check when it resumes
    (UpdateService:#asyncInit -> _attemptResume), so starting the browser
    does not talk to the update server.
  - UpdateService._selectAndInstallUpdate() offers the update to the user
    instead of downloading it, even if something claims that automatic
    updates are enabled.
  - BackgroundUpdate says so in its own words: the reason why the
    background task does nothing is that updates are manual-only by
    design, not that some policy is enabled.

The rest of the manual-only behaviour was already there:
UpdateService.manualUpdateOnly is unconditionally true (core/09), the
per-installation defaults are false (core/03) and the preferences UI hides
the automatic-install options (core/09).
